---
id: org.dxos.plugin.sandbox
name: SandboxPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

Sandbox plugin for DXOS Composer providing isolated shell environments, and the git repositories that
keep what they build.

## Backends

The operations run against `SandboxService.Service`, which the plugin contributes to the process
runtime as an application-affinity `LayerSpec`. Sandboxes run on EDGE's sandbox-service unless the
plugin's **Backend** setting is `local` (`DX_SANDBOX_BACKEND=local|edge` overrides it under Node or
Bun). Local sandboxes are processes confined by the OS sandbox (bubblewrap on Linux, Seatbelt on
macOS) via `@carderne/sandbox-runtime`:

- **Where they run**: in-process under Node or Bun. In the desktop app, whose webview cannot spawn
  processes, the plugin starts `dx-sandbox` (this package's `compile-sidecar` output) and the
  webview reaches it on a loopback port with a per-launch token passed over stdin.
- **Filesystem**: each sandbox is `$DX_SANDBOX_ROOT/<id>/` (default `~/.local/state/dxos/sandboxes`).
  Commands write only its `workspace/` (their cwd and `$HOME`) and `tmp/`; the user's home directory
  and other sandboxes are unreadable. `/workspace/…` paths in file operations map onto `workspace/`.
- **Network**: only package registries and GitHub (`DEFAULT_ALLOWED_DOMAINS`) are reachable.
- **Limits**: per-command CPU time, writable memory (Linux only) and file size, plus the wall-clock
  `timeout`, which kills the command's whole process group.
- **Environment**: the host's environment is not inherited; only `PATH`, `HOME`, `TMPDIR`, `LANG`,
  `WORKSPACE` and the operation's `env` are set.
- **Dev builds**: a desktop app bundled with `DX_ENVIRONMENT=dev` passes the source tree it was built
  from to the helper as `DX_SANDBOX_ALLOW_READ`, so commands may read its `node_modules`, `packages` and `docs`
  (not `.secrets/`, `.git/` or `.claude/` at its root) even under the home directory —
  how plugin-computer's Composer Plugin template builds against Composer's own toolchain there.

## Repositories

Sandboxes are ephemeral; a `Repository` is durable. Each is a git repository hosted by EDGE on
[Cloudflare Artifacts](https://developers.cloudflare.com/artifacts/), named after its space and object
id, so the space is part of its identity. The ECHO object is created locally and the repository on
EDGE by the first read of it, so a repository made offline, or on another device, is backed as soon
as anything looks at it.

- **Push** commits a sandbox directory (default `/workspace`; git is initialized there if needed and
  `node_modules/` is ignored) and pushes it to a branch. **Pull** checks a branch out into a sandbox
  directory, or fast-forwards it, and never overwrites local changes. Both run the container's own
  `git` with a write token EDGE mints for that one command, passes as its environment and revokes
  when it ends — the token never reaches the client.
- **Reads** (branches, log, tree, file) come from a shallow in-memory clone EDGE keeps per
  repository, fetched to 200 commits per branch, so history beyond that is not browsable.
- Only EDGE sandboxes can push or pull; a local sandbox has no route to the service's git remote.
- The article surface browses a repository: a branch picker, a lazily listed file tree beside the
  selected file, and the history, where picking a commit browses the files at it.

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.

| Term   | URI                       |
|--------|---------------------------|
| `test` | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`   |
| `op`   | `org.dxos.mdl.op@1.1`     |

## Types

```mdl
type Sandbox
  fields:
    name?: string
    baseImage?: string
    createdAt?: string
    expiresAt?: string
```

```mdl
type Repository
  fields:
    name?: string
    description?: string
    defaultBranch?: string
```

## Operations

```mdl
op createSandbox
  key: org.dxos.operation.sandbox.create
  desc: Creates a new sandbox environment persisted as an ECHO object in the space.
  input:
    name?: string
    baseImage?: string
  output:
    sandboxId: string    # ECHO object URI of the created sandbox
  effects: [echo:write, sandbox:create]
```

```mdl
op exec
  key: org.dxos.operation.sandbox.exec
  desc: Runs a shell command in the sandbox.
  input:
    sandbox: Ref<Sandbox>
    command: string
    cwd?: string
    env?: Record<string, string>
    timeout?: number
    stdin?: string
  output:
    stdout: string
    stderr: string
    exitCode: number
    success: boolean
  effects: [sandbox:exec]
```

```mdl
op uploadFile
  key: org.dxos.operation.sandbox.uploadFile
  desc: Uploads a file from ECHO into the sandbox filesystem.
  input:
    sandbox: Ref<Sandbox>
    file: Ref<File>
    path: string         # absolute path in sandbox
  output:
    path: string
  effects: [echo:read, sandbox:write]
```

```mdl
op downloadFile
  key: org.dxos.operation.sandbox.downloadFile
  desc: Downloads a file from the sandbox filesystem into ECHO.
  input:
    sandbox: Ref<Sandbox>
    path: string
    dest?: Ref<File>     # optional existing File to overwrite
  output:
    objectId: string     # ECHO object URI of the File
  effects: [sandbox:read, echo:write]
```

```mdl
op publishFiles
  key: org.dxos.operation.sandbox.publishFiles
  desc: Serves a directory of a local sandbox read-only over HTTP on this machine and returns its base URL.
  input:
    sandbox: Ref<Sandbox>
    path: string         # directory, relative to the workspace or under /workspace
  output:
    url: string          # ends in "/"; empty when it failed
    error?: string       # set iff url is empty
  effects: [sandbox:read, sandbox:serve]
```

Only the desktop app's helper publishes: it serves the directory at `http://localhost:<port>/files/<key>/`
without the bearer token, since a module loader cannot send one, so the 128-bit key minted per call is the
credential. Paths that climb out of the directory, and symlinks out of the workspace, answer 404; files are served
`nosniff` under `Content-Security-Policy: sandbox`, and keys are forgotten when the helper exits.
Under the EDGE backend, or in-process under Node, the output carries the reason instead.

```mdl
op createRepository
  key: org.dxos.operation.sandbox.createRepository
  desc: Creates a git repository persisted as an ECHO object, backed by Cloudflare Artifacts on EDGE.
  input:
    name?: string
    description?: string
    defaultBranch?: string   # default "main"
  output:
    repositoryId: string     # ECHO object URI of the created repository
    remote: string           # git remote; pushing needs a token only EDGE mints
  effects: [echo:write, repository:create]
```

```mdl
op pushToRepository
  key: org.dxos.operation.sandbox.pushToRepository
  desc: Commits a sandbox directory and pushes it to a branch of a repository.
  input:
    sandbox: Ref<Sandbox>
    repository: Ref<Repository>
    path?: string            # default /workspace
    branch?: string          # default: the repository's default branch
    message?: string
    force?: boolean          # overwrite a diverged branch
  output:
    repository: string
    branch: string
    commit?: string          # what the branch points at afterwards
    success: boolean
    output: string           # git's output, token scrubbed
  effects: [sandbox:exec, repository:write]
```

```mdl
op pullFromRepository
  key: org.dxos.operation.sandbox.pullFromRepository
  desc: Checks a branch of a repository out into a sandbox directory, or fast-forwards it.
  input:
    sandbox: Ref<Sandbox>
    repository: Ref<Repository>
    path?: string
    branch?: string
  output:
    repository: string
    branch: string
    commit?: string
    success: boolean
    output: string
  effects: [repository:read, sandbox:write]
```

```mdl
op listRepositoryBranches
  key: org.dxos.operation.sandbox.listRepositoryBranches
  desc: Lists a repository's branches and the commit each points at.
  input:
    repository: Ref<Repository>
  output:
    defaultBranch: string
    branches: { name: string, commit: string }[]
  effects: [repository:read]
```

```mdl
op getRepositoryLog
  key: org.dxos.operation.sandbox.getRepositoryLog
  desc: Lists commits newest first.
  input:
    repository: Ref<Repository>
    ref?: string             # branch or full commit hash
    limit?: number           # at most 100, default 30
    offset?: number
  output:
    commits: Commit[]
  effects: [repository:read]
```

```mdl
op listRepositoryFiles
  key: org.dxos.operation.sandbox.listRepositoryFiles
  desc: Lists a directory of a repository at a branch or commit.
  input:
    repository: Ref<Repository>
    ref?: string
    path?: string            # the root when omitted
  output:
    commit?: string          # absent for an empty repository
    entries: { name: string, path: string, type: string, hash: string, mode: string }[]
  effects: [repository:read]
```

```mdl
op readRepositoryFile
  key: org.dxos.operation.sandbox.readRepositoryFile
  desc: Reads a file of a repository at a branch or commit; binary content is base64.
  input:
    repository: Ref<Repository>
    ref?: string
    path: string
  output:
    path: string
    hash: string
    content: string
    encoding: "utf-8" | "base64"
    size: number
  effects: [repository:read]
```

## QA

Executable tests. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by test and step number.

```mdl
test QA-1: Create a sandbox and run a command
  desc: The core sandbox round-trip — create an isolated shell environment, exec a command in it.
  actors: agent
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - plugin-sandbox is enabled — it is OFF by default everywhere except dev builds (`isDev`); it
      must be enabled via Settings -> plugin registry otherwise
    - no Sandbox named "QA Sandbox" exists — ABORT rather than reusing one this test did not create
  steps:
    - name: Create the sandbox
      do: From the global action menu, choose "Create Sandbox" and name it "QA Sandbox".
      invoke: [op:createSandbox] { name: "QA Sandbox" }
      capture: created
      expect: a Sandbox named "QA Sandbox" now exists and its shell is reachable
      assert: return !!$created.sandboxId

    - name: Run a command
      do: Open the sandbox terminal and run `echo hello`.
      invoke: [op:exec] { sandbox: { "/": $created.sandboxId }, command: "echo hello" }
      expect: the terminal prints "hello" and the command exits 0
      assert: return $result.success && $result.stdout.trim() === 'hello';
  after:
    - name: Delete the sandbox
      do: Right-click "QA Sandbox" in the navtree and choose Delete.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { refs: [{ "/": $created.sandboxId }], target: $given.space }
      expect: the row leaves the navtree and the underlying shell environment is torn down
```

```mdl
test QA-2: Push a sandbox build to a repository and read it back
  desc: A sandbox's work outlives it — build in a sandbox, push to a repository, browse it, pull it into a new sandbox.
  actors: agent
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - plugin-sandbox is enabled, with the EDGE backend
    - no Sandbox or Repository named "QA Repo" exists — ABORT rather than reusing one this test did not create
  steps:
    - name: Create the sandbox
      do: Ask the assistant to create a sandbox named "QA Repo".
      invoke: [op:createSandbox] { name: "QA Repo" }
      capture: sandbox
      assert: return !!$sandbox.sandboxId

    - name: Build something
      do: Run `mkdir -p /workspace/site && echo '<h1>hi</h1>' > /workspace/site/index.html` in the sandbox.
      invoke: [op:exec] { sandbox: { "/": $sandbox.sandboxId }, command: "mkdir -p /workspace/site && echo '<h1>hi</h1>' > /workspace/site/index.html" }
      assert: return $result.success

    - name: Create the repository
      do: From the create menu, add a Repository named "QA Repo".
      invoke: [op:createRepository] { name: "QA Repo" }
      capture: repository
      expect: a Repository named "QA Repo" appears; opening it says nothing has been pushed yet
      assert: return !!$repository.repositoryId

    - name: Push
      do: Ask the assistant to push /workspace/site of the sandbox to the repository.
      invoke: [op:pushToRepository] { sandbox: { "/": $sandbox.sandboxId }, repository: { "/": $repository.repositoryId }, path: "/workspace/site", message: "QA build" }
      capture: pushed
      expect: the push reports success and a commit
      assert: return $pushed.success && /^[0-9a-f]{40}$/.test($pushed.commit)

    - name: Browse it
      do: Open "QA Repo"; the tree lists index.html, and History shows "QA build".
      invoke: [op:readRepositoryFile] { repository: { "/": $repository.repositoryId }, path: "index.html" }
      assert: return $result.content.trim() === '<h1>hi</h1>'

    - name: Pull into a fresh directory
      do: Ask the assistant to pull the repository into /workspace/copy of the sandbox.
      invoke: [op:pullFromRepository] { sandbox: { "/": $sandbox.sandboxId }, repository: { "/": $repository.repositoryId }, path: "/workspace/copy" }
      assert: return $result.success && $result.commit === $pushed.commit
  after:
    - name: Delete the sandbox and the repository
      do: Delete "QA Repo" (both) from the navtree.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { refs: [{ "/": $sandbox.sandboxId }, { "/": $repository.repositoryId }], target: $given.space }
```
